00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:51.280
mechanical or electrical trade, you can

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:53.360
cross-train by learning PLC programming

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:55.280
and automation systems. There are

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:57.320
affordable online courses that get

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:58.280
started with, but hands-on experience is

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.839
what's really going to make you

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:02.212
valuable. So, you can get certified

00:10:59.839 --> 00:11:04.440
through manufacturers like Fanuc or ABB

00:11:02.212 --> 00:11:06.600
[music] or even enter through paid

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:08.760
apprenticeship programs. Amazon, for

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:10.640
example, offers a mechatronics and

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:12.920
robotics apprenticeship where you get

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:14.440
paid while learning these exact skills.

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:16.080
Moving on, let me show you one that most

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:17.839
people overlook, but it's becoming one

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:19.720
of the most important trades in the

00:11:17.839 --> 00:11:22.320
entire country right now, and that's

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:24.440
fiber optic splicing. Now, this is not

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:26.440
old-school telecom work anymore. This is

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:28.440
critical infrastructure because right

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:31.040
now fiber demand is being driven by

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:34.200
three major things. So, data centers

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:36.640
powering AI and cloud computing, massive

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:39.520
broadband expansion across the entire

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:42.200
country, and the infrastructure behind

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:44.440
that 5G network. So, all of that runs on

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:46.480
fiber and someone has to physically

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:48.400
install it, connect it, and fix it when

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:50.440
it breaks. That's what a fiber optic

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:52.880
splicer does. So, they use precision

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:54.480
equipment to fuse fiber lines together,

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:56.920
and then they test those connections

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:58.800
using tools like the OTDR, which can

00:11:56.920 --> 00:12:00.839
literally detect a break in a line from

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:02.640
miles away. According to the National

00:12:00.839 --> 00:12:04.880
Telecommunications and Information

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:07.520
Administration, the US government has

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:10.240
committed 42 and 1/2 billion through the

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:12.560
BEAD program to expand broadband access

00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:14.640
nationwide. This means thousands of

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:17.360
miles of fiber still need to be

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:19.280
installed. Not only installed, but also

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:21.280
maintained, and that's why skilled

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:23.880
splicers are in high demand. Now, when

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:27.200
it comes to pay, many roles fall between

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:28.800
about 60,000 and 90,000 per year. That's

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:30.440
what I found. With experience,

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:32.240
especially if you're working on large

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:34.040
projects or you're traveling, that can

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:35.880
move well into six figures. And one of

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:37.640
the biggest advantages of this path is

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:39.520
how fast you can get started. The

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:41.839
industry standard certification is the

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:43.960
certified fiber optic technician through

00:12:41.839 --> 00:12:45.920
the Fiber Optic Association. So, it

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:48.720
typically takes about 3 to 5 days to

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:51.240
complete and does cost around 1,000 to

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:53.160
1,500, but no degree is required, no

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:54.760
prior experience is required, and if you

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:57.000
already have field experience, you may

00:12:54.760 --> 00:12:58.960
be able to test out at a lower cost.

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:01.760
Okay, number six and the very last one

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:03.760
on this list is a UAV drone technician.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:05.440
Now, this isn't about hobby drones. This

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:07.000
is about drones being used in real

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:09.880
industries. So, infrastructure

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:12.360
inspection, agriculture, construction,

00:13:09.880 --> 00:13:14.520
search and rescue, and even delivery.

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:16.600
Utility companies use them to inspect

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:19.200
power lines. Construction companies use

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:21.280
them to survey job sites. Farmers use

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:23.600
them for crop monitoring and precision

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:25.800
spraying. And all of those drones need

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:28.080
people who know how to operate them,

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:29.680
maintain them, and troubleshoot when

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:31.640
something goes wrong. According to the

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:34.320
Federal Aviation Administration, there

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:36.640
are already over 850,000

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:38.680
registered drones in the United States

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:40.760
with hundreds of thousands approved for

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:43.040
commercial use, and that number just

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:44.800
continues to grow year over year, which

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:46.760
means more equipment in the field and

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:48.880
more demand for skilled operators and

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:51.120
technicians. When it comes to pay, many

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:54.800
commercial drone operators start in the

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:57.160
$40,000 to $70,000 range with experience

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:59.400
or specialization like infrastructure

00:13:57.160 --> 00:14:02.960
inspection or mapping, that can move

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:05.040
into the 80 to 100K plus range. And in

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:07.400
defense or highly technical roles, it

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:09.400
can even go higher. What I like best

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:12.079
about this role is that it's one of the

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:14.440
lowest cost entry points on this entire

00:14:12.079 --> 00:14:17.360
list. To legally operate drones

00:14:14.440 --> 00:14:19.839
commercially, you need the FAA Part 107

00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:22.160
remote pilot certificate. That exam

00:14:19.839 --> 00:14:24.560
costs around $175,

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:27.480
and a prep course is usually around $100

00:14:24.560 --> 00:14:29.839
to $150, or you can just self-study

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:32.079
using free FAA materials. So, you can

00:14:29.839 --> 00:14:34.160
realistically get certified for around

00:14:32.079 --> 00:14:36.959
300 bucks, and most people will also

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:38.600
invest in like a drone, basic insurance,

00:14:36.959 --> 00:14:39.959
depending on the type of work that they

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:42.320
want to do. But, if you want to move

00:14:39.959 --> 00:14:44.720
into higher-paying maintenance or repair

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:46.959
roles, there is a more advanced path

00:14:44.720 --> 00:14:48.760
through FAA airframe and power plant

00:14:46.959 --> 00:14:50.720
certification, which is used across

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:52.600
aviation and defense. At the end of the

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:55.560
day, this is a field that's expanding

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:57.640
alongside technology. So, more drones,

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:59.640
more use cases, and more industries

00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:01.040
relying on them every single year. Okay,

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:03.200
these aren't just trends that are going

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:04.680
away. These all are accelerating, and

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:06.839
the trades are where the rubber meets

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:09.360
the road because AI can't install a

00:15:06.839 --> 00:15:11.640
cooling system in a data center. A robot

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:14.120
can't splice fiber optic cable 30 feet

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:16.520
underground. Software can't maintain a

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:18.760
grid-scale battery system in the desert.

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:21.280
